# Line endings.
#
# The repository was started on Windows without this file and with
# core.autocrlf unset, so CRLF bytes were committed verbatim into the git
# objects. Files that tooling later rewrote came back as LF, which left the
# tree split between the two and produced diffs where unrelated lines
# appeared to change.
#
# Every text file is now stored and checked out with LF. The one-off
# normalization commit is listed in .git-blame-ignore-revs, so `git blame`
# still reports the real author of each line.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets. `text=auto` detects these on its own; naming them makes the
# intent explicit and protects them if the detection ever changes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
